course: dictionary
lesson: 7956
title: Receive: getting, welcoming and spelling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To receive means to get something that someone gives or sends you. «When you receive a gift, you say thank you and maybe write a card.» The person who receives has more, and the giver has fewer. Receive can also mean to welcome guests, or to pick up a signal or call, like a radio.
explain: Look at the words around receive to find its meaning. A letter, a prize or a message can all be received. «Ownership is having the right to a thing; receiving a gift usually makes it yours.» So when you receive a bike for your birthday, the bike becomes yours.
explain: Receive is a verb, so it changes its form: receives, received, receiving. Its noun is receipt. Spelling clue: receive follows «i before e except after c», like believe and ceiling. But science, weird and height break that rule, so learn tricky words as you meet them.
fact: To receive something means to get something that someone gives or sends you.
fact: To receive people means to welcome them as guests.
fact: To receive a signal or call means to pick it up, like a radio.
fact: «Well received» means that people liked it.
fact: Receive changes form: receives, received, receiving; the noun is receipt.
exercise: «Ben was happy to receive a prize at the school show.» What does receive mean? | To hand a prize to someone else | To lose it | To hide the prize | *To get something given to you
exercise: Which spelling is correct? | recieve | receeve | *receive | recive
exercise: «Mum gave sweets to Ben and ___.» Which word completes the sentence? | I | *me | my | mine
test: «The radio can receive a signal from a station far away.» What does receive mean here? | Drop | Switch off | *Pick up | Write on
test: «Sam and ___ went to the park.» Which word completes the sentence? | my | me | mine | *I
exam: Which is the best way to show you value a gift you receive? | *Say thank you and maybe write a card | Give it straight back | Hide it away | Ask for more
